.TH EUCLID-CLI-EMM-LIST-MODULES 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-emm-list-modules \- list modules known to the Euclid manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B emm list-modules
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists every module the manager
.RI ( euclid-mgr )
knows about, as persisted in the module repository (Mongo or in-memory,
per
.IR euclid.database.backend ).
Takes no arguments.
.PP
The result is one entry per module name - not one per running process -
with an
.I instances
array holding the module's current live pool: each element is one
instance, updated in place across restarts (matched internally by a
stable instance ID, not by pid, since pid changes on every restart) and
removed once it's permanently gone (scaled down, or given up on after
exceeding its configured restart limit). The caller must be
authenticated as an administrator; see
.BR euclid-cli-emm (1)
for how that's checked.
.PP
The JSON response is printed to standard output. Each module object has:
.RS
.TP
.I name
Module name, e.g. \fIeam\fR, \fIeqs\fR, \fIesm\fR.
.TP
.I executable
Full path to the module's executable.
.TP
.I socketPath
Configured (template) Unix domain socket path; each instance's actual
socket is derived from this.
.TP
.I active
Whether the module is enabled in configuration.
.TP
.I autoRestart
Whether crashed instances are automatically restarted.
.TP
.I maxRestarts
Maximum restarts allowed per instance, or \fI\-1\fR for unlimited.
.TP
.I created ", " modified
ISO 8601 timestamps.
.TP
.I lastStartTime
ISO 8601 timestamp of when the module's pool last went from having no
running instances to having its first one - i.e. the module's own
"boot time", from which euclid-ui derives its displayed uptime.
.I null
if the module has never had a running instance. Stamped once per
cold start: if several instances come up together, or one instance
crash-restarts while a sibling stays up, this does not change - only a
transition from zero running instances to the first one updates it.
.TP
.I instances
Array of the module's current instances, each with
.IR instanceId ", " pid ", " state
(one of \fISTOPPED\fR, \fISTARTING\fR, \fIRUNNING\fR, \fISTOPPING\fR,
\fICRASHED\fR, \fIPENDING_RESTART\fR, \fIRESTARTING\fR, \fIUNKNOWN\fR),
.IR socketPath ", " restartCount ", "
and its own
.IR created "/" modified
timestamps.
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The listing was retrieved and printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
The stored session is missing or not an administrator's, the request
could not be sent, or the server rejected it. If the failure was an
expired or invalid session
.RI ( "HTTP 401" ),
the stored credentials file is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 emm list-modules
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-emm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jens Vogt <jens.vogt@opitz-consulting.com>
